  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the National Statistical System of Zambia - Capacity Building of the Central Statistical Office of Zambia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xe4;rkande av det nationella statistiksystemet i Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Ambassaden har mottagit en gemensam projektans&#xf6;kan fr&#xe5;n Zambia Statistics Agency (Zamstats) och Statistiska Centralbyr&#xe5;n (SCB) med namnet &quot;Increased access to statistics that are relevant to meet user needs&quot;. Projektetf&#xf6;rslaget har en total budget p&#xe5; SEK 44 434 000 och &#xe4;r resultat av en f&#xf6;rberedelsefas som genomf&#xf6;rts av de tv&#xe5; organisationerna under perioden februari till juli 2019 och som finansierades av Ambassaden med en budget av SEK 1 183 000.

Den f&#xf6;reslagna insatsen kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras gemensamt av Zamstats och SCB under perioden 2019 - 2023. Projektm&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att anv&#xe4;ndarna har &#xf6;kad tillg&#xe5;ng till oberoende, tillf&#xf6;rlitlig och h&#xf6;gkvalitativ statistik som publiceras i god tid, &#xe4;r korrekt och relevant och m&#xf6;ter anv&#xe4;ndarnas efterfr&#xe5;gan och behov. Projektet &#xe4;r indelat i fyra komponenter. Den f&#xf6;rsta &#xe4;r Koordinering och det f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade resultatet &#xe4;r ett st&#xe4;rkt system f&#xf6;r nationell statistik (NSS). Den andra komponenten &#xe4;r Statistikproduktion och det f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade resultatet &#xe4;r en f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad omfattning och kvalitet av Zamstats statistikproduktion. Den tredje komponenten &#xe4;r Kommunikation och spridning och det f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade resultatet &#xe4;r &#xf6;kad tillg&#xe5;ng till och f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else hos anv&#xe4;ndare av statistik. Den fj&#xe4;rde komponenten &#xe4;r ICT och det f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade resultatet &#xe4;r en existerande ICT-milj&#xf6; som st&#xf6;djer effektiv statistikproduktion.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Embassy has received a joint project proposal from Zambia Statistics Agency  and Statistics Sweden called &quot;Increased access to statistics that are relevant to meet user needs&quot;. The proposal has a total budget of SEK 44 434 000 and is the outcome of a scoping phase implemented by Zamstats and Statistics Sweden between February and July 2019 and financed by the Embassy with a budget of SEK 1 183 000.

The proposed contribution is a collaboration between the Zambia Statistics Agency and Statistics Sweden over the period 2019 - 2023. The objective of the project is that users have increased access to unbiased, reliable and quality statistics that are timely, accurate and relevant to meet their needs. The project is divided into four project components. The first component is Coordination and the expected outcome is a strengthened National Statistical System. The second component is Statistical Production and the expected outcome is improved range and quality of Zamstats&#x2019; statistical production. The third component is Communication and Dissemination and the expected outcome is increased user access and improved user understanding of existing statistics. The fourth component is Information and Communication Technology and the expected outcome is an ICT environment in place that supports efficient statistics production.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Long-term outcome (impact)
The project shall contribute to, together with other development interventions, that Policy makers in Zambia use unbiased, reliable and quality information to design polices that contribute to a sustainable development of the country.
Project Objective
Users have increased access to unbiased, reliable and quality statistics that are timely, accurate and relevant to meet user needs
Component outcomes
1. Coordination: Strengthened National Statistical System
2. Statistical production: Improved range and quality of CSO&#x2019;s statistical production
3. Communication and dissemination: Increased user access and improved user understanding of existing statistics
4. Information and Communication Technology: An ICT environment in place that supports efficient statistics production</narrative>
  </description>
